{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-108051",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${(\\frac{5}{3})}^{-3}=\\frac{27}{125}$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=\\frac{27}{125},b=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as ${log}_{5/3}⁡(\\frac{27}{125})=-3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
